{"at": "2026-07-16T00:37:45Z", "commit_ref": "none", "intent": "spec", "actor": "agent", "kind": "output", "content": "Authored spec 0042 in the two-file model (.spec-md steering + .spec-jsonl steps).\n\n.spec-md — steering narrative only. Binding constraints: deliver UI-less test(s) in Berreman/BerremanTests that reconstruct report section 7.2 (M_QZ, M_LR, M_{QZ+LR}) from rotating-analyzer intensity data and confirm the section 8 cascade identity M_{QZ+LR} approx M_LR*M_QZ (beam hits QZ first); reproduce the report first, no data-flaw tweaks; port all three reference stages (AIR calibration, glue, linear fit) and RE-DERIVE the calibration constants (rounded report values are cross-checks only); many tiny pure functions with elevated types; CSV access and the numeric least-squares solve both sit behind *Proxy records; pure F# linear least squares only (no nonlinear/LM/global optimizer, no Wolfram, no Python at test time — Python only offline once for an optional committed golden file); skip (never fail) when the sibling OPM data is absent. Named forbidden expansions listed. Parts A-E: A polarization primitives + column-major LSQ core (CRITICAL — land first); B the swappable solver seam SVC:MuellerSolverProxy; C the Mueller-data seam STORE:MuellerDataProxy; D glue + Stage-1 calibration + signal reduction; E reconstruction + the cascade identity test. References footer (Chipman, Goldstein 1992, Gil 2016, Lu-Chipman 1996, MathNet, ALGLIB).\n\n.spec-jsonl — 11 forward-only steps. Contracts: SVC:MuellerSolverProxy (ADD step 3 declare record + SolverError + LeastSquaresSolution + mock; IMPLEMENT step 4 real createMathNetSvd via vendored MathNet SVD, both in OpticalConstructor.Domain) and STORE:MuellerDataProxy (ADD step 5 declare MuellerRawRow + MuellerDataError + proxy in Domain reusing Experiments.DataFilePath; IMPLEMENT step 6 pure parseMuellerCsv + file-backed createFileBacked in OpticalConstructor.Storage). Plain IMPLEMENT steps add a new Domain module MuellerReconstruction (Retardance + retarderMueller; kron4/vecColumnMajor/muellerOfVecColumnMajor/frobeniusDiff; label parse + family/kind + source/analyzer models + effective states + designRow; Stage-1 cosine fits + closed-form retardance; dark-subtract + per-family AIR gain; buildDesign/reconstruct/cascadeProduct). Final WIRE step 11 wires the real proxies in BerremanTests, loads the five science CSVs + darkness/bullshit checks from the relative OPM path (SkippableFact), runs Stage 1->2->3, and asserts the section 7.2 matrices (~2e-3, rank 16) + section 8 metrics (Frobenius ~0.571, mean|d| ~0.113, max|d| ~0.268, largest diffs at (4,2),(2,2)).\n\nEvery cited pointer verified by Read against the working tree: Propagation.fs (muellerOfRows:35, muellerElement:40, analyzerMueller:73, identityMueller:99, rotationMueller:117, rotateMueller:128, compoundMueller:139), Fields.fs (StokesVector:580, MuellerMatrix:598, M*M op:651), Geometry.fs (Angle:34, RealVector4:128), ExperimentDataProxy.fs:43, ExperimentDataStore.fs (loadThrough:34, createFileBacked:51), SpectralImport.fs:46, Experiments.fs (DataFilePath:142), MuellerMatrixTests.fs (assertMuellerEqual:20), MatrixComparison.fs (allowedDiff:13), AlglibAdapter.fs:20, and the vendored MathNet MultipleRegression at MathNetNumerics/Numerics/LinearRegression/MultipleRegression.cs.\n\nSource read: specs/0042/.manual/004-mueller-inverse-reconstruction-test.md (plus 001-task.txt, 003-comments.txt).\n"}
